  "preamble": "Diphthongization of the high front vowel [i] (usually long [iː]) to [ei], the first step of a lowering path that often continues to [ai]. It occurred in Common Czech (Standard /iː/ ý > ej: mlýn > mlejn), and in Cantonese, whose vernacular readings turn Middle Chinese -ij into -ei (四 sijH > sei3).",
